    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 24 October, the erection of a roof extension, comprising a hip to gable conversion measuring 2.6 metres perpendicular height, 4.35 metres wide and 8.8 metres deep and a rear dormer measuring 5.34 metres wide, 2.17 metres deep and 3.02 metres high was not lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe development falls outside the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the volume of the roof extension, single storey rear extension, covered rear area , porch and front canopy results in the proposal exceeding the permitted development limit.  \r\n"
